# Backup policy — {{.Name}}

<!-- ISO/IEC 29110 WP.12. The stated policy line the standard asks for; the
     machinery already exists. -->

Everything that matters is committed: source, the derived contract artifacts,
the requirement files, this file. The pushed remote IS the backup, and
recovery is `git clone` — an agent that dies loses nothing that matters.

- Remote(s): TODO (the canonical push target; add mirrors here if any)
- Cadence: every landing is pushed; nothing lives only on one machine
- Recovery drill: `git clone` + `task test` proves the repo restores; the
  first `go test ./...` bootstraps any artifact a fresh clone lacks
- Out of scope: production DATA backups belong to the deployment's ops
  runbook, not this repo
